-- title:
--   Newform multiplicity in a local corner of H¹(Γ₀(N),𝒪)
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology, with finite residue field $k$, and write $\bar K$ for `AlgebraicClosure (FractionRing 𝒪)`. Let $S$ be a finite set of primes, $N\ge 1$ a level all of whose prime divisors lie in $S$. On $H=$ [`CohCarrier.H1 N ⊤ 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L162), the additive homomorphisms from $\Gamma_0(N)$ (as [`CohCarrier.GammaH N ⊤`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133)) to $\mathcal{O}$, consider the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily N ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) indexed by [`CohCarrier.Gen N S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13): the transfer operators [`CohCarrier.heckeTL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) at primes $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and at primes $q\mid N$, and the diamond operators [`CohCarrier.diamondL`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L55) at $d\in(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$; they are assumed to commute pairwise. Let $\bar\theta$ assign to each generator a value in $k$, and let `Sp` be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) (a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal spectrum and satisfying $e_i\in\mathfrak{m}_j\iff i\neq j$) of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal{O}}(H)$ generated by these operators. Fix an index $i_0$ and an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0}Be_{i_0}$ to $k$ sending the image of each operator to the corresponding value of $\bar\theta$, and assume every element of the corner submodule $e_{i_0}H$ is parabolic, i.e. vanishes on all $\gamma$ with $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2=4$. Let $M_g\mid N$, let $g$ be a newform of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem occurs at no proper divisor of $M_g$), let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb{C}$ taking each $T_\ell$ ($\ell\nmid M_g$) and each $U_q$ ($q\mid M_g$) to the corresponding $q$-expansion coefficient of $g$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\bar K$. Assume that for each prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ the element $\iota(a_\ell(g))$ is a root of a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ whose reduction is $(X-\bar\theta(T_\ell))^{\deg}$. Then the $\bar K$-dimension of the intersection of the range of the base change to $\bar K$ of the inclusion $e_{i_0}H\hookrightarrow H$ with the intersection, over all primes $\ell\notin S$ not dividing $N$, of the $\iota(a_\ell(g))$-eigenspaces of the base-changed [`CohCarrier.heckeTL N ⊤ 𝒪 ℓ`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23) equals $2\prod_{q\mid N}c_q$, where for each prime $q\mid N$ one puts $a_q=\iota(\chi_g(U_q))$ if $q\mid M_g$ and $a_q=\iota(\chi_g(T_q))$ otherwise, $e=v_q(N)-v_q(M_g)$, $P_q=X-a_q$ if $e=0$ and $P_q=X^{e-1}\bigl(X^2-a_qX+(q\text{ if }q\nmid M_g\text{, else }0)\bigr)$ if $e>0$, and $c_q$ is the sum of the multiplicities in $P_q$ of those roots $x$ that satisfy a monic polynomial over $\mathcal{O}$ reducing to $(X-\bar\theta(U_q))^{\deg}$, the other roots contributing $0$.
--
--   This is the dimension count underlying the newform-multiplicity computation for a local corner of $H^1(\Gamma_0(N),\mathcal{O})$: it expresses the size of the simultaneous $T_\ell$-eigenspace attached to a newform $g$ of level $M_g\mid N$ inside the base-changed corner as $2$ (for the two periods) times a product of local oldform contributions, each counted only when it is residually compatible with $\bar\theta$ at the corresponding $U_q$. It feeds [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.newformMultiplicity_finrank_iInf_eigenspace_algebraicClosure_eq_of_isCornerRealization_level_self), the multiplicity statement used in the freeness argument for Hecke modules.
